UPDATE team SET sort_order = 1, team_group = 'office', status = 'published' WHERE slug = 'carie-broecker';
UPDATE team SET sort_order = 2, team_group = 'office', status = 'published', role_title = 'Development Director', bio = 'Cameron shares her home with two rescued animals: her dog, Pomela Anderson, who came to her from Animal Friends Rescue Project as a medical foster and never left, and a bunny from the SPCA who happily roams the living room.

Cameron started at POMDR as our Clinic Manager on May 11, 2020. In March 2021, she stepped into the role of Operations Manager, overseeing the daily complexities of rescue intake, medical coordination, and program logistics. In May 2024 she became our Behavior and Enrichment Manager, helping to build and strengthen POMDR''s dog behavior program to support dogs with more complex needs. After a four-month hiatus, Cameron joined the POMDR Board of Directors.

In 2026, she stepped off the board to serve as POMDR''s Interim Development Director, and then quickly made the move permanent, bringing her deep institutional knowledge, long-standing commitment to the organization, and strong relationship-building skills into this critical leadership role. Her experience across operations, behavior, and board service gives her a comprehensive understanding of POMDR''s mission, programs, and impact -- an invaluable asset in working with donors, sponsors, and community partners.

Professionally, Cameron trained dolphins and sea lions for the U.S. Navy Marine Mammal Program in Washington state. She then worked as an Animal Care Specialist at the Monterey Bay Aquarium, rescuing and rehabilitating sea otters. Throughout her career, she has developed strengths in leadership, cross-functional collaboration, public engagement, training, and high-stakes decision-making, skills that translate naturally into strategic development work and donor stewardship. Her past volunteer work includes the Seattle Aquarium, the Oregon Coast Aquarium, the Alaska SeaLife Center, and a Humane Society wildlife rehabilitation center, working with animals from harbor seals and sea otter pups to raccoons, raptors, and even a baby long-tailed weasel. Locally, she volunteered with AFRP at the adoption center and as a foster for medical cases.

Cameron graduated from Western Washington University with a Bachelor of Science in Biology. While working for the Navy, she learned to conduct closed-circuit SCUBA diving.' WHERE slug = 'cameron-donegan';
UPDATE team SET sort_order = 3, team_group = 'office', status = 'published' WHERE slug = 'allison-mckee';
UPDATE team SET sort_order = 4, team_group = 'office', status = 'published', bio = 'Caitlin''s current pack includes three senior pups adopted from POMDR plus two cats and six rabbits. There''s the most senior, a Yorkie named Jack; his BFF Tater Tot, a Shih-Tzu/Chihuahua mix; and Frodo, a very silly Maltese mix. The two kitties, Thomas and Luke, came from a shelter in Sacramento. The six rescued rabbits -- Walter, Nilla, Teddy, Maisy, Charlotte, and Clancy -- play host to a constant stream of foster bunnies. Add to that any foster dogs passing through.

Before joining the POMDR staff in November 2019, Caitlin volunteered for multiple wildlife rehabilitation facilities and an educational nature center in the Sacramento area. She also volunteered locally with the Sea Otter Research and Conservation program at the Monterey Bay Aquarium and Golden Oldies Cat Rescue as their volunteer coordinator and has served on the board of directors. Caitlin is currently involved with multiple rabbit rescue groups across California. Previously, she has worked in education with special needs students and as a middle school science teacher, at the SPCA of Monterey County as a barn specialist, and as a wildlife biologist for an environmental consulting company.

Caitlin originally started with POMDR as a Kennel Attendant but took on the role of Adoptions Coordinator in July 2021 and in May 2024, Caitlin moved into the Operations Manager role.

She graduated from CSU Monterey Bay with a Bachelor of Science degree in Biology and a Single Subject Science Teaching Credential.' WHERE slug = 'caitlin-lupien';
UPDATE team SET sort_order = 5, team_group = 'office', status = 'published', bio = 'Andrew shares his home with two rescued dogs: Sydney, a sweet Golden Retriever/Australian Shepherd/Labrador Retriever mix, and Pepper, an Australian Shepherd/Labrador Retriever mix he adopted from POMDR.

He has always had multiple rescued pups in his home, so he was excited to join the POMDR staff in February 2024 to promote the work we do with dogs.

Andrew has worked at a digital advertising agency and also has worked as a freelance web and graphic designer, a social media coordinator, and a UI/UX (user interface and user experience) designer for websites.

He earned a Bachelor of Arts degree in Product Design at the University of Oregon, where he was on the Dean''s List at the Allied Arts and Architecture School. While in a design class there, he received a monetary Lighting Design Award.' WHERE slug = 'andrew-zielinski';
UPDATE team SET sort_order = 6, team_group = 'office', status = 'published' WHERE slug = 'shanel-parolini';
UPDATE team SET sort_order = 7, team_group = 'office', status = 'published' WHERE slug = 'alejandra-raya';
INSERT INTO team (name, slug, role_title, team_group, bio, photo_url, image_key, sort_order, status) SELECT 'Nisha Addleman', 'nisha-addleman', 'Behavior Coordinator', 'office', 'Nisha shares her home with Toby, a rescued brindle Mountain Cur who joined her family in Colorado Springs, and Raisin, a black Lab service dog from Monkey Tail Ranch in Hollister.

She grew up with rescued dogs and cats and has a passion for helping animals in need. In fact, she never had a non-rescued animal until she got Raisin, her service dog, in 2024. She joined the POMDR staff in April 2026.

Before joining POMDR, Nisha worked at Monkey Tail Ranch, training service dogs and therapy dogs for various facilities such as schools and courtrooms. She also led group training and helped with individual training.

Nisha holds Associate''s degrees in Psychology and Creative Writing from Monterey Peninsula College. She is currently working on attaining her CPDT-KSA (Certified Professional Dog Trainer-Knowledge and Skills Assessed) and hopes to finish it by the end of the year. In the fall, she will begin studies at Arizona State University (online) for her Bachelor''s degree in Psychology and will start their accelerated Master''s program in Psychology with a focus on research.', 'https://www.peaceofminddogrescue.org/images/people/aboutus/NishaAddleman.jpg', 'https://www.peaceofminddogrescue.org/images/people/aboutus/NishaAddleman.jpg', 8, 'published' FROM DUAL WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM team WHERE slug = 'nisha-addleman');
INSERT INTO team (name, slug, role_title, team_group, bio, photo_url, image_key, sort_order, status) SELECT 'Courtney Young', 'courtney-young', 'Adoptions Coordinator', 'office', 'Courtney shares her home with two rescued dogs: Carmen, a spunky Miniature Pinscher mix, and Benny, a charming little Chiweenie.

Before joining the POMDR staff in May of 2026, Courtney volunteered with POMDR for about five years. During that time, she was a dog transporter, a handler at adoption events, a dog walker with our Helping Paw Program, a BE Buddy and a foster. Before that, she volunteered at Hearts Therapeutic Equestrian Center in Santa Barbara as a lesson assistant and part of their barn crew.

Prior to her involvement with POMDR, she worked primarily in health care. This included roles as a medical assistant, caregiver and patient coordinator.

Courtney holds a Bachelor of Science degree in Public Health with a focus in Health Education from Cal State Chico. She has various certificates related to health care such as Infection Control and Dental Practices. She also obtained her Yoga Teacher Certification and completed a 200-hour Yoga Teacher Training in India.', 'https://www.peaceofminddogrescue.org/images/people/aboutus/CourtneyYoung.jpg', 'https://www.peaceofminddogrescue.org/images/people/aboutus/CourtneyYoung.jpg', 9, 'published' FROM DUAL WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM team WHERE slug = 'courtney-young');
INSERT INTO team (name, slug, role_title, team_group, bio, photo_url, image_key, sort_order, status) SELECT 'Briana Ryan', 'briana-ryan', 'Volunteer Coordinator', 'office', 'Briana shares her home with an adorable black Chug (Chihuahua/Pug) named Bean, adopted from POMDR.

Before joining our staff in June 2024, Briana had been volunteering with POMDR for about two years, leading adoption events, fostering dogs, and organizing fundraising events, including our Pilates, Pups and Pints series. She was involved in dog rescue even before that, volunteering with a local dog rescue in New York City before moving to California.

Briana spent nine years in business operations in the technology/venture capital sector. She now employs her organizational and problem-solving skills to help senior dogs and senior people, a mission she is deeply passionate about. She is also a dedicated runner and can often be found on the local trails. She has been running ultramarathons for the past six years and has completed distances up to 100 miles!

Briana holds a Bachelor''s degree in Psychology from the University of Florida and a Master''s degree in Mental Health Counseling from CUNY John Jay.', 'https://www.peaceofminddogrescue.org/images/people/aboutus/BrianaRyan.jpg', 'https://www.peaceofminddogrescue.org/images/people/aboutus/BrianaRyan.jpg', 10, 'published' FROM DUAL WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM team WHERE slug = 'briana-ryan');
UPDATE team SET sort_order = 1, team_group = 'benefit-shop', status = 'published', role_title = 'Benefit Shop Manager' WHERE slug = 'carmelita-garcia';
UPDATE team SET sort_order = 1, team_group = 'clinic', status = 'published', bio = 'Dr. Erin shares her home with Brooklyn, a Labrador Retriever, and Berley, a Samoyed. The newest member of her pack is Ozzy, a Chihuahua/Basset Hound mix adopted from POMDR.

She came to POMDR in July 2023. While in veterinary school at Iowa State University, she was an active member in the Shelter Medicine Club and helped facilitate low-income vaccine clinics in Des Moines. She also volunteered for the Josh & Friends Project, benefiting children in hospitals and utilizing the human-animal bond to encourage sick adolescents during their treatments. She has volunteered at shelters and free vaccine clinics across the country and helped facilitate a spay/neuter and preventive care clinic for animals in South Dakota.

Before coming to POMDR, Dr Erin worked as a small animal general practitioner in Ankeny, Iowa.

She completed her Bachelors degree in Biology and attained her Doctor of Veterinary Medicine at Iowa State University.' WHERE slug = 'dr-erin-trannel';
