Nougat was found as a stray and brought to Santa Clara County Animal Services. The shelter reached out to POMDR to help this senior gentleman find the right home for his next chapter. Now he''s ready to settle in, find his favorite lap, and make himself very much at home.', short_description = 'Nougat is a sweet little guy with a real talent for finding the best seat in the house - usually right next to you, or preferably in your lap!', looks_like = 'Chihuahua mix', sex = 'Male', age_years = 11, weight_lbs = 12, sponsored_by = 'Joan Best', intake_date = COALESCE(intake_date, '2025-02-20'), is_draft = 0, is_active = 1, needs_review = 0, is_courtesy = 0, is_available = 1, is_adopted = 0, is_hospice = 0, is_foster_needed = 0, is_temp_foster_needed = 0, is_adoption_pending = 0, foster_start_date = NULL, foster_end_date = NULL WHERE id = 76 AND name = 'Nougat';
-- Casper (adoptable; matched by Shelterluv number)
UPDATE animals SET name_public = IF(COALESCE(name_public, '') = '', 'Casper', name_public), description = 'Meet Casper, the friendly pup! This senior lad is full of energy and loves to play with toys. He is a joyful guy with a big heart who is happy to tag along wherever you go. Sadly, Casper was recently diagnosed with lymphoma. Without treatment, his prognosis is only a few months to live. We are choosing to give him the best chance possible, so he is undergoing cancer treatment at a specialist in the Monterey area. Based on his energy and enthusiasm, you would never know he is fighting a serious illness! If his adopters are willing to continue bringing him to treatment appointments in Monterey post-adoption, POMDR will cover the cost of his treatment (approx. 288 days).

While Casper is very friendly and social, he is working on resource guarding from both people and other dogs. While he does well with his foster pup sibling, we think he would also love to be an only dog where he doesn''t have to share his toys. Casper does great around cats. He is looking for a forever home where he can float right into your heart (and toy bin).

Handsome Casper joined us from the Animal Resource Center of the Inland Empire. He was brought in as a stray. Due to his senior status, they felt he would do best in a senior focused rescue.', short_description = 'Meet Casper, the friendly pup! This senior lad is full of energy and loves to play with toys. He is a joyful guy with a big heart who is happy to tag along wherever you go.', looks_like = 'Yorkshire Terrier', sex = 'Male', age_years = 11, weight_lbs = 14, intake_date = COALESCE(intake_date, '2025-09-16'), is_draft = 0, is_active = 1, needs_review = 0, is_courtesy = 0, is_available = 1, is_adopted = 0, is_hospice = 0, is_foster_needed = 0, is_temp_foster_needed = 0, is_adoption_pending = 0, foster_start_date = NULL, foster_end_date = NULL WHERE id = 60 AND name = 'Casper';
-- Bumper Car (adoptable; matched by Shelterluv number)
UPDATE animals SET name_public = IF(COALESCE(name_public, '') = '', 'Bumper Car', name_public), description = 'Bumper Car is just the perfect blend of sweet and spunky! Bumper Car may be blind, but she sees the world with her heart- and what a big, beautiful heart it is. Whether she''s following the sound of your voice or curling up beside you for snuggles, Bumper Car is all about connection. Despite her vision loss, she''s a confident little navigator who quickly learns her surroundings. Her sense of smell and hearing are top-notch, and she uses them like a pro to explore, adapt, and find her favorite cozy spots.

She gets along beautifully with other dogs and cats, and her gentle energy makes her a joy to be around. If you''re looking for a lovable sidekick who will warm your heart, make you laugh, and remind you daily that joy has no limits -Bumper Car is your girl.

Bumper Car came to us from the Sacramento Animal Shelter after being found as a stray, but you''d never guess her past by her joyful spirit. She''s already left the shelter life in her past and is ready to settle into a forever home where she''ll be cherished for the sweet little treasure she is.', short_description = 'Bumper Car is just the perfect blend of sweet and spunky! Bumper Car may be blind, but she sees the world with her heart- and what a big, beautiful heart it is.', looks_like = 'Shih Tzu, Maltese mix', sex = 'Female', age_years = 11, weight_lbs = 20, sponsored_by = 'JudyLeRoy, Fran A. Palacio', intake_date = COALESCE(intake_date, '2024-12-04'), is_draft = 0, is_active = 1, needs_review = 0, is_courtesy = 0, is_available = 1, is_adopted = 0, is_hospice = 0, is_foster_needed = 0, is_temp_foster_needed = 0, is_adoption_pending = 0, foster_start_date = NULL, foster_end_date = NULL WHERE id = 80 AND name = 'Bumper Car';
-- Jamesy Boy [Recently Adopted] (adoptable; matched by Shelterluv number)
UPDATE animals SET name_public = IF(COALESCE(name_public, '') = '', 'Jamesy Boy', name_public), description = 'Jamesy Boy is a tiny gentleman with a soft spirit and the sweetest gray muzzle. During the day, Jamsey will be your constant buddy. He loves to follow his foster parent around the house, but knows how to stay out of the way of your feet! He is a super cuddly boy who sleeps through the night and even does well when left home alone.

Despite his age, Jamesy Boy still has plenty of pep for a gentle walk and perks right up when treats or affection are on the menu. He is polite, easy to please, and grateful for every bit of kindness shown to him. This little guy has known some tough days, but his resilience and tenderness shine through every time he nudges your hand for pets. Jamesy will also gladly hang out in a pouch or sling and would love to go on adventures this way! Jamesy does excellently with other dogs, he is a respectful and confident member of the pack in his foster home!

Darling Jamesy Boy joined us from the Contra Costa Animal Shelter when they reached out for placement with a senior focused rescue.', short_description = 'Jamesy Boy is a tiny gentleman with a soft spirit and the sweetest gray muzzle. During the day, Jamsey will be your constant buddy.', looks_like = 'Chihuahua mix', sex = 'Male', age_years = 12, weight_lbs = 7, intake_date = COALESCE(intake_date, '2025-11-15'), is_draft = 0, is_active = 1, needs_review = 0, is_courtesy = 0, is_available = 0, is_adopted = 1, adopted_date = COALESCE(adopted_date, CURDATE()) WHERE id = 45 AND name = 'Jamesy Boy';
-- Huey (hospice; matched by Shelterluv number)
UPDATE animals SET name_public = IF(COALESCE(name_public, '') = '', 'Huey', name_public), description = 'Huey is an old soul who has mastered the art of being a very goodest of boys. Sweet Huey joined us from the Animal Resource Center of the Inland Empire after he was found as a stray. Due to their over full shelter, they felt he would to best in the hands of a rescue that could help ensure he landed in the right adoptive home.

Sadly, shortly after his arrival with us, Huey''s health began to decline. After a few emergency vet visits and testing, his medical team suspect an intestinal cancer is the reason for the decline. We''re so grateful that Huey has the support of our vet team and his loving foster home to meet his needs in this challenging time where he will remain for the rest of his days.Please consider sponsoring Huey''s forever care.', short_description = 'Huey is an old soul who has mastered the art of being a very goodest of boys. Sweet Huey joined us from the Animal Resource Center of the Inland Empire after he was found as a stray.', intake_date = COALESCE(intake_date, '2026-08-12'), is_draft = 0, is_active = 1, needs_review = 0, is_courtesy = 0, is_available = 1, is_adopted = 0, is_hospice = 1, is_foster_needed = 0, is_temp_foster_needed = 0, is_adoption_pending = 0, foster_start_date = NULL, foster_end_date = NULL WHERE id = 2240 AND name = 'Huey';
